From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 20:20:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] mfd: max77705: Accept the second revision of the chip

The driver was written against a chip reporting the third revision and
refuses every other one.  The Galaxy S10+ carries the second, so the whole
companion chip of its main PMIC, the fuel gauge and the charger with it,
is turned away at probe.

Everything this driver touches is the same in that revision.  Read from the
phone over the bus: the identity register answers 0x15 and the revision
register 0x02, the register map answers over its whole range, and with the
check relaxed the fuel gauge and the charger both come up and report sane
values.  The revisions differ in the firmware image the vendor loads into
the USB-C part of the chip, which is not something this driver has any
business with.

Signed-off-by: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/mfd/max77705.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mfd/max77705.c b/drivers/mfd/max77705.c
index e98c76d6b69..c53f21f5444 100644
--- a/drivers/mfd/max77705.c
+++ b/drivers/mfd/max77705.c
@@ -105,7 +105,15 @@ static int max77705_i2c_probe(struct i2c_client *i2c)
 		return -ENODEV;
 
 	pmic_rev = pmic_rev_value & MAX77705_REVISION_MASK;
-	if (pmic_rev != MAX77705_PASS3)
+	/*
+	 * The driver was written against a chip reporting the third revision.
+	 * The Galaxy S10+ carries the second one, and everything this driver
+	 * touches is the same in it: the identity register reads back 0x15, the
+	 * register map answers over its whole range, and the two revisions
+	 * differ only in the firmware image the vendor loads into the USB-C
+	 * part, which is not something this driver has any business with.
+	 */
+	if (pmic_rev != MAX77705_PASS2 && pmic_rev != MAX77705_PASS3)
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, -ENODEV, "Rev.0x%x is not tested\n", pmic_rev);
 
 	/* Active Discharge Enable */
